From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: local accounts load their network profile

At sign-in Chrome asks session_manager to load the user's shill profile
(the load-shill-profile event, shill_login_user), once user network
policy has been applied: UserNetworkConfigurationUpdaterAsh votes
PasswordConsumingService::kNetwork and UserSessionManager loads the
profile, in the session's first Chrome only (StartSessionType kPrimary).
A Chrome restarted after a crash picks the session up without
StartSession() (kNone) and skips it, the first Chrome having loaded the
profile already.

A local account's session runs in the Chrome that restarted as its Linux
user (0008), which picks the session up that way, and the login screen's
Chrome restarted before network policy was applied. So shill never had
the user's profile: networks not shared with other users (the default
for secured Wi-Fi) failed with "Error configuring network", and per-user
VPNs and certificates had nowhere to go. That Chrome now loads it when
the primary user is a local account; loading it again is harmless.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ash/login/session/user_session_manager.cc b/chrome/browser/ash/login/session/user_session_manager.cc
index 42de977d943c6..40ed4933aa97b 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ash/login/session/user_session_manager.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ash/login/session/user_session_manager.cc
@@ -1419,6 +1419,23 @@ void UserSessionManager::VoteForSavingLoginPassword(
   CHECK_LT(service, PasswordConsumingService::kCount,
            base::NotFatalUntil::M161);
 
+  // NickelOS: a local account's session runs in the Chrome that restarted as
+  // its Linux user, which picks the session up the way it does after a crash
+  // (no StartSession(): kNone), and the Chrome before it never got this far:
+  // the session's shill profile is loaded here, or the user's own networks
+  // (and anything else in that profile) cannot be saved.
+  if (service == PasswordConsumingService::kNetwork &&
+      start_session_type_ == StartSessionType::kNone) {
+    const user_manager::User* primary =
+        user_manager::UserManager::Get()->GetPrimaryUser();
+    if (primary && user_manager::IsNickelLocalAccount(primary->GetAccountId())) {
+      base::SingleThreadTaskRunner::GetCurrentDefault()->PostTask(
+          FROM_HERE, base::BindOnce(&UserSessionManager::LoadShillProfile,
+                                    GetUserSessionManagerAsWeakPtr(),
+                                    primary->GetAccountId()));
+    }
+  }
+
   // VoteForSavingLoginPassword should only be called for the primary user
   // session. It also should not be called when restarting the browser after a
   // crash, because in that case a password is not available to chrome anymore.
